# What the arm64 buildd chroot of the Ubuntu suite needs for the ffmpeg
# and ffprobe (scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh; lib-buildd.sh makes the
# chroot). One package per line where there is a comment, several on a line
# where the comment covers them; "#" starts a comment.
#
# Every library here is named in the `options` of scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh:
# FFmpeg is configured with --disable-autodetect, so a package that is
# installed but not enabled changes nothing, and an enabled option without
# its package stops the configure. The hardware video codecs are the V4L2
# M2M ones of the iris video core, built into FFmpeg; libdrm is for the DRM
# device context their decoder patches export frames through. There is no
# other hardware acceleration in the build, on purpose.
build-essential pkg-config file
# threads and TLS come from glibc and libssl: https, and SRT on TLS
libssl-dev libsrt-openssl-dev
# video: H.264, HEVC, VP8 and VP9, AV1 (libaom, SVT-AV1 and rav1e to encode,
# dav1d to decode), JPEG 2000, Theora, XviD
libx264-dev libx265-dev libvpx-dev libaom-dev libsvtav1enc-dev librav1e-dev libdav1d-dev
libopenjp2-7-dev libtheora-dev libxvidcore-dev
# still images: WebP, JPEG XL
libwebp-dev libjxl-dev
# audio: Vorbis, Opus, MP3, the SoX resampler, AMR narrowband and wideband
libvorbis-dev libopus-dev libmp3lame-dev libsoxr-dev libopencore-amrnb-dev libopencore-amrwb-dev
# subtitles and text: libass; drawtext with fontconfig, FriBidi and HarfBuzz
libass-dev libfreetype-dev libfontconfig-dev libfribidi-dev libharfbuzz-dev
# filters: time stretching, stabilisation, the colour space conversion of zscale
librubberband-dev libvidstab-dev libzimg-dev
# compression, and the DRM device context
zlib1g-dev libbz2-dev liblzma-dev libdrm-dev
